1
00:00:53,136 --> 00:00:57,474
Let's see if you can fight in the dark.

2
00:00:58,141 --> 00:00:59,559
Show me your cat-like abilities.

3
00:01:12,155 --> 00:01:13,782
You really are a shameless woman.

4
00:01:13,865 --> 00:01:15,533
Remember this until the afterlife.

5
00:01:15,617 --> 00:01:18,036
I will never let your soul rest.
Remember that!

6
00:01:49,025 --> 00:01:50,151
In Tagalog,

7
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:51,945
one bullet is all it takes.

8
00:01:52,028 --> 00:01:52,904
Mikoy.

9
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,406
This is my fight.

10
00:02:12,215 --> 00:02:15,093
Hey, stop, or else I'll really kill you.

11
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:35,238
Mikoy, don't!

12
00:04:34,315 --> 00:04:35,400
That was fun, wasn't it?

13
00:04:35,483 --> 00:04:37,026
Did you enjoy that, sir?

14
00:04:38,903 --> 00:04:40,113
Are you trying to get yourself killed?

15
00:04:40,196 --> 00:04:42,156
You're being so dramatic.

16
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,574
We were just having fun.

17
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:46,035
Having fun?

18
00:04:46,577 --> 00:04:47,537
Didn't you see this?

19
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:49,163
That's not my Adam's apple.

20
00:04:49,247 --> 00:04:50,790
My balls went up here.

21
00:04:50,873 --> 00:04:53,418
Even the eggs I had for breakfast,
I threw them up!

22
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:56,713
You're so dramatic.

23
00:04:56,796 --> 00:04:57,964
Just get on.

24
00:04:58,047 --> 00:04:59,757
Let's go back to base. Get on.

25
00:04:59,841 --> 00:05:01,843
If you want, you can go by yourself.

26
00:05:03,052 --> 00:05:04,262
I don't want to die yet!

27
00:05:04,345 --> 00:05:06,180
Suit yourself.

28
00:05:07,265 --> 00:05:09,058
Suit yourself, too.

29
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:17,817
Hey, hey! Where are you going?

30
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:19,152
Hey!

31
00:05:19,986 --> 00:05:21,195
What are you doing?

32
00:05:21,279 --> 00:05:22,864
Go on! Go!

33
00:05:22,947 --> 00:05:24,032
Fine!

34
00:05:30,705 --> 00:05:33,708
Hey. Hey! Hey!

35
00:05:33,791 --> 00:05:35,335
Come back here!

36
00:05:35,418 --> 00:05:37,795
Hey!

37
00:05:52,351 --> 00:05:55,104
I heard you left our customer
in the middle of nowhere?

38
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:57,315
Why? What's the problem?

39
00:05:59,108 --> 00:06:00,401
Chiara, I'm talking to you.

40
00:06:00,985 --> 00:06:01,903
What happened?

41
00:06:02,904 --> 00:06:04,906
Chiara, I'm talking to you.

42
00:06:06,199 --> 00:06:08,076
Are you thinking or doing this on purpose?

43
00:06:10,661 --> 00:06:12,872
Mikoy, we were having
a perfectly good conversation.

44
00:06:12,955 --> 00:06:14,415
What's with all this lovey-dovey stuff?

45
00:06:14,499 --> 00:06:15,458
Huh?

46
00:06:16,501 --> 00:06:18,836
Why? What did my sweetheart do?

47
00:06:19,462 --> 00:06:21,881
Why don't you ask Chiara

48
00:06:21,964 --> 00:06:24,675
how she turned my ATV adventure
into an extreme sport?

49
00:06:25,301 --> 00:06:26,385
What?

50
00:06:26,469 --> 00:06:29,013
Maybe she just turned your adventure
business into a real adventure?

51
00:06:30,807 --> 00:06:33,601
Mikoy, I have no problem with adventure.

52
00:06:35,269 --> 00:06:36,771
But Chiara is different.

53
00:06:36,854 --> 00:06:38,689
Whenever I take her as my tour guide,

54
00:06:38,773 --> 00:06:40,566
I feel like I'm in
a permanent danger zone!

55
00:06:48,908 --> 00:06:51,327
I admit I did go
a little too fast earlier,

56
00:06:51,410 --> 00:06:52,912
but it wasn't my fault!

57
00:06:52,995 --> 00:06:54,288
So whose fault was it?

58
00:06:54,997 --> 00:06:57,041
The ATV you bought was powerful.

59
00:06:57,125 --> 00:07:00,837
So I just unleashed its power
to its full potential.

60
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:02,588
So it's my fault, Chiara?

61
00:07:02,672 --> 00:07:04,215
It won't happen again.

62
00:07:04,298 --> 00:07:05,258
It was her first time.

63
00:07:05,341 --> 00:07:07,552
What do you mean, first time?
What about what she did the other day?

64
00:07:08,886 --> 00:07:10,221
I guess I can't do this. Sorry.

65
00:07:10,304 --> 00:07:11,639
I'm just going to get off. I'm scared now.

66
00:07:11,722 --> 00:07:14,183
- Oh my God, please. Sorry.
- No. You can do it.

67
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:15,476
No, I really can't.

68
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:18,146
I really can't. I'm just going to get off.

69
00:07:18,229 --> 00:07:20,231
Come on. Please? Sorry.

70
00:07:20,314 --> 00:07:22,400
And you know, you know how I'm feeling?

71
00:07:22,483 --> 00:07:23,985
I'm genuinely terrified right now.

72
00:07:24,068 --> 00:07:26,696
Please, let me get off!

73
00:07:35,538 --> 00:07:38,416
It was just that one time, I promise!

74
00:07:38,499 --> 00:07:39,625
It was only that one woman.

75
00:07:39,709 --> 00:07:42,628
She deserved that treatment.
She was annoying.

76
00:07:42,712 --> 00:07:44,881
What about what you did
to my senior citizen companions?

77
00:07:44,964 --> 00:07:46,799
Did they deserve that treatment too?

78
00:07:51,262 --> 00:07:53,347
And who said you could stop?

79
00:07:53,431 --> 00:07:55,516
We need to hurry, don't we?

80
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,852
We need to catch the sunset.

81
00:07:57,935 --> 00:08:00,771
Why did you even hike if you weren't
going to make it to the focal point?

82
00:08:00,855 --> 00:08:01,981
Good grief, girl.

83
00:08:02,064 --> 00:08:03,691
We can't do this anymore.

84
00:08:03,774 --> 00:08:06,652
At this rate, heaven might take us
because of all this suffering.

85
00:08:06,736 --> 00:08:09,906
Well, Grandpa, that's exactly
what's going to happen

86
00:08:09,989 --> 00:08:11,449
if that's what you keep thinking.

87
00:08:12,950 --> 00:08:17,914
If you think you're young and strong,
you will feel young and strong!

88
00:08:17,997 --> 00:08:19,165
Oh, girl!

89
00:08:19,248 --> 00:08:21,417
We don't need to see that sunset anymore.

90
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:23,669
We don't need it anymore. Bye!

91
00:08:30,843 --> 00:08:33,513
They're so weak! You're all so weak!

92
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:38,935
Well, I explained everything properly.

93
00:08:39,018 --> 00:08:40,102
I warned them

94
00:08:40,186 --> 00:08:42,688
about what to expect on the hike.

95
00:08:42,772 --> 00:08:44,315
But they insisted.

96
00:08:44,398 --> 00:08:47,568
They insisted, and then they're the ones
who kept complaining!

97
00:08:47,652 --> 00:08:51,447
That attitude of yours is going
to ruin my business!

98
00:08:52,156 --> 00:08:53,908
Don't you know that
the customer is always right?

99
00:08:57,662 --> 00:09:00,498
especially when they're abusive
and ill-mannered.

100
00:09:02,542 --> 00:09:03,501
There.

101
00:09:03,584 --> 00:09:05,753
Sir Pandoy, I'm really sorry.

102
00:09:06,295 --> 00:09:07,588
Let me talk to Chiara.

103
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:24,897
We coordinated
with the Italian authorities.

104
00:09:24,981 --> 00:09:25,982
But for now,

105
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:27,942
it seems they're avoiding it.

106
00:09:28,025 --> 00:09:31,904
They don't want the complication
of handling La Morte Bianca's remains.

107
00:09:31,988 --> 00:09:34,365
Her reputation in Italy
is also a sensitive matter.

108
00:09:34,448 --> 00:09:37,076
So we can say that they
don't want it to seem

109
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:39,036
like they had anything
to do with her death.

110
00:09:56,762 --> 00:10:00,141
But most of them have either been arrested
or are on the run.

111
00:10:00,224 --> 00:10:03,019
But the moment
they cross into another territory,

112
00:10:10,443 --> 00:10:12,069
So is it safe to say

113
00:10:12,153 --> 00:10:15,197
that we have completely dismantled
the Concordat?

114
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:34,800
<i>This organization is still extensive, sir.</i>

115
00:10:34,884 --> 00:10:38,471
<i>And it's just a matter of time</i>
<i>before new leadership emerges.</i>

116
00:10:38,554 --> 00:10:41,724
<i>Luckily, we managed to freeze</i>
<i>most of their major accounts</i>

117
00:10:41,807 --> 00:10:42,683
<i>while they were asleep,</i>

118
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:45,394
<i>and we didn't just cripple them. Ouch!</i>

119
00:10:45,478 --> 00:10:49,023
<i>It looks like we paralyzed</i>
<i>their entire organization. Victory!</i>

120
00:10:49,106 --> 00:10:49,982
<i>I'm cute!</i>

121
00:10:50,066 --> 00:10:54,612
<i>But I'm getting more handsome</i>
<i>because I'm part of G.A.G.O!</i>

122
00:10:58,115 --> 00:11:01,410
And as time goes by,

123
00:11:01,494 --> 00:11:03,537
their world keeps getting smaller.

124
00:11:11,796 --> 00:11:15,049
Well, rehabilitation does have
its merits, right?

125
00:11:15,132 --> 00:11:16,509
Especially for people

126
00:11:16,592 --> 00:11:18,803
who have a chance to change.

127
00:11:18,886 --> 00:11:21,138
Like this person.

128
00:11:23,933 --> 00:11:26,060
They say people don't change.

129
00:11:27,019 --> 00:11:29,397
Are you sure about that, Agent Sianong?

130
00:11:32,525 --> 00:11:36,112
If these two mess up again,
I'll personally have them arrested.

131
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:40,616
That's harsh! Come on, chill!

132
00:11:40,699 --> 00:11:44,495
Agent Alex, it's like our history
means nothing to you!

133
00:11:53,462 --> 00:11:55,506
<i>They are currently in our custody.</i>

134
00:11:56,090 --> 00:11:59,468
<i>Their lawyers are appealing</i>
<i>for mitigating circumstances,</i>

135
00:11:59,552 --> 00:12:00,594
<i>arguing that, in the end,</i>

136
00:12:01,345 --> 00:12:04,598
<i>they helped dismantle</i>
<i>the Concordat and La Morte Bianca.</i>

137
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:12,022
They might have other information

138
00:12:12,106 --> 00:12:14,275
that they can provide
in exchange for other leads.

139
00:12:14,358 --> 00:12:15,901
Information that may still be held
by the loose elements

140
00:12:15,985 --> 00:12:17,820
of the Concordat and La Morte Bianca.

141
00:12:20,906 --> 00:12:22,158
And what did they say?

142
00:12:22,783 --> 00:12:24,577
They said they had nothing else to offer.

143
00:12:24,660 --> 00:12:26,245
Or they don't want to talk anymore

144
00:12:26,328 --> 00:12:29,081
because they've lost their power,

145
00:12:29,165 --> 00:12:32,293
and their lives will be in danger.

146
00:12:56,692 --> 00:12:57,443
Not that one.

147
00:12:57,526 --> 00:13:01,822
The elephant I'm talking about
is Mikoy and Chiara.

148
00:13:04,658 --> 00:13:06,785
Where are Mikoy and Chiara?

149
00:13:17,171 --> 00:13:19,006
Sir Pandoy is wrong

150
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:22,551
because the customers he's catering to

151
00:13:22,635 --> 00:13:25,012
are just pampered tourists!

152
00:13:25,095 --> 00:13:28,182
The kind whose only concern
is posting on Fishbook.

153
00:13:28,265 --> 00:13:33,354
Not customers who are looking
for a real experience.

154
00:13:35,481 --> 00:13:39,193
He's attracting low-quality customers.

155
00:13:40,444 --> 00:13:43,948
If that's the target market he wants
to cater to with his business,

156
00:13:44,031 --> 00:13:45,282
that's his choice.

157
00:13:45,366 --> 00:13:47,117
It's none of our business, sweetheart.

158
00:13:48,619 --> 00:13:50,162
That's why he's boring.

159
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:56,835
Well, you know, sometimes,

160
00:13:57,461 --> 00:13:59,004
boring is better.

161
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:07,221
Just think about everything
we've been through this past year.

162
00:14:09,723 --> 00:14:10,766
I've met my quota.

163
00:14:10,849 --> 00:14:13,018
I'd rather have a somewhat

164
00:14:13,644 --> 00:14:14,895
boring life.

165
00:14:15,729 --> 00:14:16,730
That's all.

166
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:19,024
So why did you choose me?

167
00:14:24,321 --> 00:14:27,199
With all the complications in my life?

168
00:14:27,283 --> 00:14:29,285
With my complicated past?

169
00:14:32,371 --> 00:14:34,498
Sweetheart, what are you talking about?

170
00:14:36,083 --> 00:14:38,377
Isn't that what you're trying to say?

171
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:40,880
That all I bring you is a headache?

172
00:14:42,298 --> 00:14:44,341
That's not what I'm saying, sweetheart.

173
00:14:44,425 --> 00:14:47,177
Even if you don't say it,
that's the truth.

174
00:14:47,261 --> 00:14:49,305
That's how I feel.

175
00:14:49,388 --> 00:14:51,515
Like I'm becoming exhausting to be around.

176
00:14:52,474 --> 00:14:53,559
Oh, sweetheart.

177
00:14:53,642 --> 00:14:55,144
You know, that's what's difficult
about you sometimes.

178
00:14:55,227 --> 00:14:57,396
Your imagination goes off
in all directions,

179
00:14:57,479 --> 00:14:59,815
and you read all kinds of meanings
into everything.

180
00:15:00,566 --> 00:15:02,610
I don't regret choosing you.

181
00:15:03,944 --> 00:15:05,112
Not at all.

182
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:25,966
At least I'm not boring!

183
00:15:27,051 --> 00:15:28,010
Right?

184
00:15:28,093 --> 00:15:29,720
Like this.

185
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:33,432
Chili with ice cream.

186
00:15:33,515 --> 00:15:35,476
Do you think it makes sense

187
00:15:35,559 --> 00:15:37,728
to put chili in ice cream?

188
00:15:40,022 --> 00:15:42,983
It's not supposed to make sense,
but that's life.

189
00:15:43,817 --> 00:15:46,320
You need something new every now and then.

190
00:15:46,403 --> 00:15:48,572
You need a little adventure.

191
00:15:48,656 --> 00:15:50,658
Not something boring,
not something that's always the same.

192
00:15:56,372 --> 00:15:57,665
What?

193
00:15:57,748 --> 00:15:59,541
I'm walking out, okay?

194
00:15:59,625 --> 00:16:00,501
I know.

195
00:16:02,169 --> 00:16:03,796
You're not going to stop me?

196
00:16:04,922 --> 00:16:06,632
You're just going to let me leave?

197
00:16:07,466 --> 00:16:08,592
You're cute.

198
00:16:27,611 --> 00:16:29,405
Where are Mikoy and Chiara?

199
00:16:52,011 --> 00:16:54,930
Is there no way to speed up
your internet connection?

200
00:16:56,932 --> 00:17:00,686
The office's internet plan was downgraded

201
00:17:00,769 --> 00:17:03,522
due to budget cuts.

202
00:17:04,231 --> 00:17:05,899
And someone here

203
00:17:05,983 --> 00:17:08,110
is hogging the internet

204
00:17:08,193 --> 00:17:11,822
by illegally downloading
movies and series.

205
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:14,408
Here we go.

206
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:26,003
<i>And today's topic is…</i>

207
00:17:31,175 --> 00:17:33,844
<i>Let's say your airplane crashes.</i>

208
00:17:39,266 --> 00:17:42,686
So you need to do
everything you can to survive.

209
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:44,063
<i>Let's go this way.</i>

210
00:17:44,146 --> 00:17:45,939
<i>I hear something over here.</i>

211
00:17:49,777 --> 00:17:50,944
There.

212
00:17:51,028 --> 00:17:54,114
Listen to your surroundings.

213
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:59,369
<i>I can feel the vibration of the ground.</i>

214
00:17:59,453 --> 00:18:01,163
The sound is getting louder.

215
00:18:01,246 --> 00:18:02,873
The shaking is getting stronger.

216
00:18:02,956 --> 00:18:04,792
Mother Earth’s heartbeat.

217
00:18:06,210 --> 00:18:08,003
Hey, what are you doing down there?

218
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:09,463
You might get hit by a coconut,

219
00:18:09,546 --> 00:18:10,964
and you're trespassing here.

220
00:18:11,965 --> 00:18:12,883
Sorry.

221
00:18:24,394 --> 00:18:26,897
No wonder he has so many followers.

222
00:18:26,980 --> 00:18:29,233
What does this have to do
with Mikoy and Chiara?

223
00:18:29,316 --> 00:18:30,943
Just keep watching.

224
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:36,740
<i>That brother is so grumpy.</i>
<i>It's not like his coconut is even good.</i>

225
00:18:37,282 --> 00:18:38,200
There.

226
00:18:38,283 --> 00:18:40,661
So, guys, now we're going
to continue our search

227
00:18:40,744 --> 00:18:43,205
for a body of water.

228
00:18:43,288 --> 00:18:44,289
Because

229
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:47,167
if you listen carefully,

230
00:18:48,335 --> 00:18:50,045
you can feel it in the ground

231
00:18:50,129 --> 00:18:52,256
when you're close to a body of water.

232
00:18:52,339 --> 00:18:53,423
<i>Like a…</i>

233
00:18:54,258 --> 00:18:55,134
<i>river.</i>

234
00:18:55,843 --> 00:18:56,969
<i>Or a stream.</i>

235
00:18:57,678 --> 00:18:59,138
<i>Or a river.</i>

236
00:19:00,931 --> 00:19:02,057
<i>Are those the same thing? River?</i>

237
00:19:02,558 --> 00:19:04,601
Yes, they're the same.
River is just English.

238
00:19:06,311 --> 00:19:07,604
There it is!

239
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:09,690
What a coincidence.

240
00:19:09,773 --> 00:19:10,691
A river!

241
00:19:17,239 --> 00:19:18,323
<i>It's fresh!</i>

242
00:19:26,331 --> 00:19:30,127
<i>I will teach you how to catch fish.</i>

243
00:19:31,461 --> 00:19:32,296
<i>One more.</i>

244
00:19:40,053 --> 00:19:41,096
<i>Got one!</i>

245
00:19:47,519 --> 00:19:49,229
Are you done having fun?

246
00:19:49,313 --> 00:19:52,316
I thought you wanted to know what
really happened to Mikoy and Chiara.

247
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:01,533
<i>Got you!</i>

248
00:20:01,617 --> 00:20:03,160
<i>Look how big it is!</i>

249
00:20:03,243 --> 00:20:06,663
<i>So, assuming you catch</i>
<i>a fish in the river, you're set!</i>

250
00:20:06,747 --> 00:20:08,582
<i>You're good to go.</i>

251
00:20:08,665 --> 00:20:11,084
<i>All you need to do</i>
<i>is find a way to cook the fish,</i>

252
00:20:11,627 --> 00:20:13,003
<i>but if you can't,</i>

253
00:20:13,086 --> 00:20:15,380
<i>just eat it raw!</i>

254
00:20:15,464 --> 00:20:17,049
<i>Like sashimi.</i>

255
00:20:17,132 --> 00:20:18,258
<i>Like sashimi, like in Japan.</i>

256
00:20:18,342 --> 00:20:19,468
- <i>Rhamboy.</i>
- <i>Right?</i>

257
00:20:20,135 --> 00:20:21,428
- <i>What are you doing?</i>
- <i>Aunt Tess.</i>

258
00:20:21,511 --> 00:20:22,888
<i>I'm vlogging.</i>

259
00:20:22,971 --> 00:20:24,681
- <i>What are you doing</i>
- <i>I tried…</i>

260
00:20:24,765 --> 00:20:25,974
<i>with that enormous fish?</i>

261
00:20:26,058 --> 00:20:29,061
<i>I tried catching fish</i>
<i>in the river earlier.</i>

262
00:20:29,144 --> 00:20:32,064
<i>But it was too difficult,</i>
<i>so I just bought one as a prop.</i>

263
00:20:38,654 --> 00:20:40,906
<i>Welcome to Sito Harong!</i>

264
00:20:40,989 --> 00:20:43,617
<i>Life here is simple, but it's abundant.</i>

265
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:44,910
<i>Abundant.</i>

266
00:20:44,993 --> 00:20:47,454
<i>Not because we have a lot of money.</i>

267
00:20:47,537 --> 00:20:54,086
<i>It's abundant because</i>
<i>we're willing to share!</i>

268
00:20:54,169 --> 00:20:56,630
- <i>Mommy Tess, Tito Mario, hello!</i>
- <i>Hey!</i>

269
00:20:58,131 --> 00:20:59,508
My boys!

270
00:21:04,930 --> 00:21:05,806
Smelled the food.

271
00:21:05,889 --> 00:21:06,890
Look at you!

272
00:21:06,974 --> 00:21:08,016
Hi, guys! Hi, guys!

273
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:09,268
This is what you're good at!

274
00:21:09,351 --> 00:21:11,728
Earlier, I needed people to carry things

275
00:21:11,812 --> 00:21:13,438
and help set things up,
and you were nowhere to be found.

276
00:21:13,522 --> 00:21:16,066
Now that there's nothing left to do,

277
00:21:16,149 --> 00:21:18,318
- here you are.
- You saw the food, and here you are!

278
00:21:18,402 --> 00:21:19,319
Right?

279
00:21:19,403 --> 00:21:21,238
But I did clean the drainage canal.

280
00:21:22,072 --> 00:21:23,615
<i>You said you were brushing your teeth.</i>

281
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:24,825
<i>I said drainage canal.</i>

282
00:21:25,534 --> 00:21:26,535
How about the hole on our roof?

283
00:21:26,618 --> 00:21:28,787
Isn't that your job?

284
00:21:28,870 --> 00:21:30,163
<i>Wait a minute!</i>

285
00:21:30,247 --> 00:21:33,625
<i>So this is the new love team of the year!</i>

286
00:21:33,709 --> 00:21:36,545
<i>Brother Mikoy and Chiara!</i>

287
00:21:40,674 --> 00:21:42,759
<i>Come here, come here. Okay, okay.</i>

288
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:44,803
<i>Well, well, well!</i>

289
00:21:44,886 --> 00:21:46,638
<i>Is this the one you caught in the river?</i>

290
00:21:46,722 --> 00:21:49,891
Oh, come on. That's what I've been saying.
Here's another one.

291
00:21:49,975 --> 00:21:53,186
Maya-maya aren't caught in freshwater.

292
00:21:53,270 --> 00:21:56,106
They're caught in saltwater.

293
00:21:56,189 --> 00:21:58,025
- There!
- In the sea!

294
00:21:58,108 --> 00:21:59,026
And to be honest,

295
00:21:59,109 --> 00:22:01,320
I just bought this at the local market.

296
00:22:01,403 --> 00:22:02,654
Right.

297
00:22:02,738 --> 00:22:05,657
It's just really hard to catch fish.

298
00:22:05,741 --> 00:22:08,493
I've already gone through Plan A, Plan B,
and this is already Plan C!

299
00:22:08,577 --> 00:22:09,578
Yes.

300
00:22:09,661 --> 00:22:12,247
Well, there are techniques for that.

301
00:22:12,331 --> 00:22:13,790
Do you want me to teach you?

302
00:22:13,874 --> 00:22:14,791
Wow!

303
00:22:14,875 --> 00:22:16,877
Teach him? Really?

304
00:22:17,461 --> 00:22:18,462
Don't!

305
00:22:18,545 --> 00:22:21,006
Who knows what else
you might learn from Chiara?

306
00:22:25,719 --> 00:22:29,473
Rhamboy, you won't just learn
how to catch fish from Chiara.

307
00:22:30,098 --> 00:22:32,601
You'll also learn
how to catch Mikoy's heart.

308
00:22:32,684 --> 00:22:35,103
- There you go!
- Wow!

309
00:22:35,187 --> 00:22:36,855
Good one. My turn, my turn.

310
00:22:36,938 --> 00:22:40,192
As for me, what I learned from Chiara

311
00:22:40,984 --> 00:22:43,028
was how to keep gulping and gulping,

312
00:22:43,111 --> 00:22:44,362
outdoing even the…

313
00:22:46,823 --> 00:22:48,492
You're hilarious. You're hilarious.

314
00:22:48,575 --> 00:22:50,035
All right, come on, everyone.

315
00:22:50,118 --> 00:22:53,497
- Help me out, so we can get this done.
- Okay.

316
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:56,625
Chiara, you're good
at chopping vegetables, right?

317
00:22:56,708 --> 00:22:57,793
- Come help me.
- Right, right. Come sit here.

318
00:22:57,876 --> 00:22:59,211
You three, come here.

319
00:22:59,294 --> 00:23:00,962
There's a list inside.

320
00:23:01,046 --> 00:23:03,006
Get it. There's still some shopping to do.

321
00:23:03,090 --> 00:23:04,883
Get the money from Mario. Hurry.

322
00:23:04,966 --> 00:23:06,093
Uncle Mario!

323
00:23:06,176 --> 00:23:07,135
Why me?

324
00:23:07,219 --> 00:23:09,554
Of course. You're the head of the family,
aren't you?

325
00:23:20,023 --> 00:23:21,024
With his profile,

326
00:23:21,108 --> 00:23:23,735
we know that even though
he's just starting out,

327
00:23:23,819 --> 00:23:26,238
he easily adapts to any situation.

328
00:23:31,743 --> 00:23:35,580
Okay, if not because of being bored,
maybe because I feel like I’m stuck.

329
00:23:35,664 --> 00:23:38,333
<i>There you go!</i>

330
00:23:38,416 --> 00:23:40,043
<i>I’m happy.</i>

331
00:23:40,127 --> 00:23:41,378
<i>It’s just,</i>

332
00:23:41,461 --> 00:23:42,754
<i>he seems like he doesn’t have a plan.</i>

333
00:23:42,838 --> 00:23:43,797
<i>Plan about what?</i>

334
00:23:48,218 --> 00:23:51,680
You have to understand Chiara’s situation.

335
00:23:51,763 --> 00:23:55,767
Think about the frustration
of being alone without your family.

336
00:23:55,851 --> 00:23:57,018
But I’m here.

337
00:23:57,102 --> 00:23:59,938
But it’s inevitable to feel

338
00:24:00,021 --> 00:24:04,860
that she’s alone in this new life.

339
00:24:06,862 --> 00:24:08,363
I have good news.

340
00:24:08,446 --> 00:24:09,573
Something happened to Mikoy.

341
00:24:10,282 --> 00:24:11,199
What?

342
00:24:11,283 --> 00:24:14,202
He’s in the ecopark,
at the top of the mountain.

343
00:24:15,328 --> 00:24:16,454
Chiara.

344
00:24:19,624 --> 00:24:21,126
I’m coming, Mikoy.

345
00:24:22,460 --> 00:24:24,254
<i>What is happening to you?</i>
